+"R1","storage/data durability","minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-15 creates only the orders table and minisvc/cli.py:7-12 is the only code path that calls init_schema()","HTTP writes and reads can fail at runtime if the app starts without the CLI bootstrap having created the table","Run schema init in app startup and add a startup check or migration step","service owner for startup/bootstrap"
+"R2","audit behavior","minisvc/audit.py:4-10 returns an event dict only; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-29 has no audit table or audit insert","There is no durable audit trail for create or read actions, which weakens traceability and incident review","Add an audit repository/table or drop durable-audit claims from docs and ops runbooks","service owner for compliance/observability"
+"R3","configuration/runtime environment","minisvc/config.py:10-14 defaults MINISVC_DB to relative path orders.sqlite and parses MINISVC_READONLY, but minisvc/cli.py:7-12 and minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 do not enforce readonly","Runtime behavior depends on current working directory, and operators may think readonly mode prevents writes when it does not","Use an explicit absolute DB path in deployment config and enforce readonly in the write path","service owner for config and deploy"
+"R4","API input validation","minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 indexes payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int(...) without validation or error mapping","Bad or missing input can raise raw exceptions, which may leak as 500 responses in the embedding HTTP layer","Validate payload shape and types before building Order and map failures to client errors","API owner"
+"R5","write reliability","minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 calls repo.save(order) once; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 does one SQLite insert with no retry or exception handling","A transient SQLite lock or I/O failure causes an immediate failed request with no bounded retry path","Add bounded retry only for known transient failures and add tests around failure handling","storage owner"
+"R6","data integrity and conflict handling","minisvc/storage/repo.py:20-21 inserts directly into a primary-key table with no duplicate handling","Duplicate order_id requests raise SQLite integrity errors and may produce poor client-facing behavior","Catch integrity errors and return a stable conflict response or enforce idempotency","API and storage owners"
